{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Betzalel son of Uri son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah, made.</b> 'Made' means he gave instruction to the craftsmen who performed the work to make it, for he himself made only the Ark alone. Therefore his name was singled out there, where it is written (Exodus 37:1): ״ויעש בצלאל את הארון״. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: even in matters his master had not told him, his judgment concurred with what was said to Moses at Sinai." "<b>And by way of the Midrash.</b> Betzalel and Oholiav were the most expert craftsmen of them all — Betzalel from the tribe of Judah, which is called גור אריה (a lion's whelp), and Oholiav from the tribe of Dan, which is called דן גור אריה. And the Temple resembled a lion, for we find that the Sanctuary was narrow at its rear and broad at its front, resembling a lion, as it is written (Isaiah 29:1): ״הוי אריאל אריאל קרית חנה דוד״. And by a lion they were punished, as it is said (Jeremiah 4:7): ״עלה אריה מסבכו״. And by a lion they are destined to prevail in the time of salvation, as it is said (Micah 5:7): ״והיה שארית יעקב בגוים כאריה בבהמות יער״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:07:46.521072116Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}